"Reimagining advertising with AI | OpenAI (https://openai.com/index/reimagining-advertising-with-ai/)\nciteturn814view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://openai.com/index/reimagining-advertising-with-ai/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 158\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n‎Gemini Apps’ release updates & improvements (https://gemini.google/release-notes/)\nciteturn814view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn811view2\",\"pattern\":\"2026.09\"}); Total lines: 1324\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:   * cite1†For Students L3:   * Features\nL4: \nL5:     * cite2†Gemini Live L6:     * cite3†Image Generation L7:     * cite4†Video Generation L8:     * cite5†Music Generation L9:     * cite6†Deep Research L10:     * cite7†Gemini Spark L11:     * cite8†Personal Intelligence L12:     * cite9†Daily Brief L13:     * cite10†Canvas L14:     * cite11†Gemini in Chrome L15: \nL16:   * cite12†Explore L17:   * cite13†Subscriptions L18:   * What's New\nL19: \nL20:     * cite14†Gemini for desktop L21:     * cite15†Gemini Drops L22:     * cite16†Latest News L23: \nL24:   * cite17†Try Gemini†gemini.google.com L25: \nL26: # Release Notes\nL27: ## 2026.09.10\nL28: ### Bring Google Gemini to your PC with the new Windows app\nL29:   * What: The Gemini app is now available on Windows. Press Alt + Space to summon Gemini instantly from anywhere on your PC whenever you need it. You can get quick answers, draft messages, and brainstorm ideas right alongside your active applications. Inside your dedicated desktop workspace, you have access to everything you love about Gemini.\nL30: You can connect to Google apps like Gmail and Google Drive to summarize documents and find information quickly, generate custom images with Nano Banana, and dive into in-depth research on any topic.\nL31: The app is available on Windows 10 or later. Download it today at cite14†gemini.google/desktop .\nL32: \nL33:   * Why: Your desktop is where you get work done. Bringing Gemini straight to your PC with instant shortcut access keeps you in your flow, making it simple to get answers and create visuals right alongside your everyday tools.\nL34: ## 2026.08.19\nL35: ### A new dedicated student hub, study notebooks on mobile, one year of Google AI Pro in the US, or Google AI Plus in 140+ countries at no cost.\nL36:   * What: We’re introducing a dedicated student hub in the Gemini app to help students easily manage classes and create personalized study notebooks from their own course materials like syllabi. Study notebooks—first launched on desktop in June—are now available on mobile to help students get organized, prepare for class and stay on top of their material. Plus, eligible college students can get one year of Google AI Pro in the US, or Google AI Plus in 140+ countries at no cost.\nL37:   * Why: By bringing study notebooks to mobile, creating a centralized student hub, and providing a student plan, we are helping students learn with a personalized study partner.\nL38: \nL39: Eligible students only. cite18†Offer Terms†one.google.com apply. Redeem until December 31, 2026. Automatically renews at the standard monthly price for the applicable Google AI Plan included in your Offer. Cancel anytime.\nL40: ## 2026.07.29\nL41: ### Create and edit with your voice, anywhere on your desktop with Gemini on macOS\nL42:   * What: We’re introducing a new way to work with Gemini using just your voice, right where you are. Press and hold the Fn key to dictate into your active window and have Gemini transcribe your spoken words into clean, polished text directly at your cursor. You can also enable Gemini reasoning in the app settings to do even more based on screen context—such as highlighting text to rewrite or reformat it, selecting local files to extract information, or generating images anywhere you want.\nL43: The new feature is rolling out today in English to all users on the Gemini macOS app. Download the app at cite19†gemini.google/mac .\nL44: \nL45:   * Why: Speaking your thoughts lets you work at the speed of thought—allowing you to ramble, hesitate, or self-correct while Gemini seamlessly makes sense of it. By taking in your screen context and outputting results directly at your cursor in any app, Gemini works right alongside you to keep you in your flow.\nL46: ## 2026.07.21\nL47: ### 3.6 Flash: An upgraded model for your daily life\nL48: \nL49:   * What: We’re introducing Gemini 3.6 Flash, an upgraded version of our Flash model, to help you tackle everyday tasks. Try using it for quick tasks like analyzing several documents or multi-step projects like building a working prototype with the Canvas tool.\nL50: \nL51: We're excited to bring this model to all Gemini app users globally. To access, select \"3.6 Flash\" in the model drop down.\nL52:   * Why: We want to make Gemini the most helpful AI assistant for everyone. With Gemini 3.6 Flash, you can now tackle your everyday tasks with greater confidence, without choosing between speed and quality.\nL53: ## 2026.06.30\nL54: ### Hand off the heavy lifting to Gemini Spark, now available in the macOS app\nL55: \nL56:   * What: Gemini Spark, your personal AI agent, is coming to the Gemini app for macOS. It helps you navigate your digital life by working on tasks on your behalf. Operating autonomously and under your direction, it organizes folders, uses your local files to build documents, and handles complex workflows across Google Workspace.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe AI Daily Brief: Artificial Intelligence News and Analysis - Podcast - Apple Podcasts (https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-ai-daily-brief-artificial-intelligence-news/id1680633614)\nciteturn814view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: